 func _ready() -> void :
 
+	# [MP8] ================ Version handshake ================
+	#
+	# Both vanilla backends **already have** a version check. The client sends `Globals.game_version` along,
+	# and if it doesn't match, the host calls `refuse_client_rpc(..., RefuseReason.VersionMismatch)`
+	#(`enet_backend.gd:133` / `steam_backend.gd:169`).
+	# Adding a mod suffix to it gets us three things for free.
+	#   ① Vanilla players can't join mod lobbies, and mod players can't join vanilla lobbies.
+	#   ② **Different mod versions refuse each other too**.
+	#   ③ It uses the game's own refusal UI, instead of "you get in but the RPCs don't match, and things go haywire halfway through".
+	# Mixed installs are the biggest fear for a mod that changes core scripts, and vanilla hands us this gate for free.
+	#
+	# ⚠️ The cost (an informed choice) is that **with the mod installed you can't play with friends on vanilla**,
+	# and you have to go back and restore with the installer's `install_mp8.ps1 -Uninstall`.
+	#
+	# ⚠️ Why this is written here instead of patching `autoloads/globals.gd` —
+	# that file is 553 lines, decompiled, and has never once been verified by recompiling,
+	# so pulling all of it into the patch surface for one string isn't worth it. This file has been verified by dozens of 8-player test matches.
+	# **It depends on autoload order**. `Globals` (project.godot line 20) comes
+	# **before** `NetworkManager` (line 24), so it can be read and modified from here.
+	# The version string is only read **during the connection handshake**, so changing it this early is always in time.
+	#
+	# When releasing a new mod version, change MP8_VERSION_TAG — people on older versions get cleanly kept out.
+	# The version number in the main menu's bottom-right corner (`main_menu.gd:66`) shows it too,
+	# so you can tell at a glance whether the other side has the mod installed and whether it's the same version.
+	if not Globals.game_version.contains(MP8_VERSION_TAG):
