+
+	# [MP8] Lock the capacity guard — this must be the very last thing in _ready() (see the comment on _mp8_cap_locked for why).
+	# [MP8] **Before** locking, first pull capacity back to the value we settled on.
+	#
+	# Why this step is required (a hole found by testing on 2026-09-03, not by reasoning).
+	# The engine loads autoloads in two passes — first _init on all of them (registering the global constants), then _ready on all of them.
+	# The loader (MPML) comes first, and its _ready synchronously calls each mod's _mod_ready.
+	# At that moment this node's _ready hasn't run and the lock isn't on yet, but the global constant `NetworkManager`
